WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.146 --> 00:00:00.979
(light music)

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:01.870
- [Narrator] If you're having trouble

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.290
finding Mr. or Mrs. Swipe
Right, it might be time

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.143
to turn to matchmaking's
ancient roots, literally.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.500
Because deep in a forest in Germany stands

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.050
a 600 year-old oak tree
that has introduced hundreds

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.986
of single people.
(light music)

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:20.415
(bell dings)

00:00:20.415 --> 00:00:23.415
(light piano music)

00:00:29.042 --> 00:00:30.480
(dreamy music)

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.090
It all began around 1890 when
the forest ranger's daughter

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.963
met a chocolate maker from Leipzig.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.875
The father did not approve
of their relationship.

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:41.890
(dreamy music)

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.330
They had to find a way
to exchange messages,

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.700
so they used a tree about 300 feet away

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.433
from the forest ranger's office.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.740
A branch had broken off, forming a hole,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.172
and it was there they put their letters.

00:00:54.172 --> 00:00:55.990
(girl laughs)
(owl hoots)

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.090
Once her father learned
how they were secretly

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:02.110
communicating, he finally
approved of their relationship.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.100
They married under the
tree on June 2nd, 1891,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.619
after which the tree became
known as Bridegroom's Oak.

00:01:09.619 --> 00:01:13.786
(Karl speaks in foreign language)

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.910
And people still send letters
to the tree to this day.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.557
But can you truly find a life partner

00:01:32.557 --> 00:01:34.570
for the price of postage?

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.803
No one knows better than Karl-Heinz.

00:01:38.286 --> 00:01:42.453
(Karl speaks in foreign language)

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.269
But there was one letter
that caught his eye.

00:02:31.269 --> 00:02:35.436
(Karl speaks in foreign language)

00:03:19.428 --> 00:03:22.011
(dreamy music)

